# Copy to .env (gitignored) and set your values. The signing/notarization tooling
# asks the installed csec broker for these App Store Connect references. A first
# build on a Mac with no csec yet reads them with 1Password's CLI instead, so
# they must then be op:// references.
# Compatible shorthand for an item with key_id, issuer_id and key (.p8) fields:
OP_ASC_ITEM="op://<Vault>/<Item Title>"
# Used only by that first build, when 1Password has more than one account;
# csec owns provider selection once installed.
# OP_ACCOUNT="my.1password.com"
# Alternatively, set all three canonical refs explicitly (any supported backend):
# ASC_KEY_ID_REF="csec://signing/key-id"
# ASC_ISSUER_ID_REF="csec://signing/issuer-id"
# ASC_KEY_REF="csec://signing/private-key"

# Optional overrides. build-and-install.sh defaults to Stateful Ltd's two
# Developer ID identities for the team in identity.xcconfig ("Developer ID
# Application: Stateful Ltd (TEAMID)" and "Developer ID Installer: ...") and to
# packaging/build/convenient-security.mobileprovision. A build under your own
# team names its certificates as `security find-identity -v` shows them:
# SIGN_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)"
# INSTALLER_IDENTITY="Developer ID Installer: Your Name (TEAMID)"
# PROFILE_PATH=packaging/build/convenient-security.mobileprovision
# The iPhone to install the approval app onto, by name, UDID or devicectl
# identifier. Needed only when more than one paired iPhone is available.
# CSEC_IPHONE_DEVICE="My iPhone"
